    <h1>Why is the sky blue?</h1>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- English Column -->
        <div class="column">
            <div class="section">
                <h2>For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</h2>
                <p>The sky is blue because the sunlight loves to play! When the sunlight reaches the Earth, it hits the air and bounces around like everywhere. The blue light is short and bouncy, so it spreads out everywhere in the sky. So, when you look up, you see all that blue light bouncing at you!</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h2>For a High School Teenager</h2>
                <p>The sky is blue because of something called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of all the colors of the rainbow. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it hits gas molecules and small particles in the air. Blue light travels in shorter, smaller waves than red light. Because of this, it gets scattered in much more directions than the other colors, which is why we see a blue sky during the day.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h2>For a Physics PhD</h2>
                <p>The blue color of the sky is primarily due to Rayleigh scattering—the scattering of electromagnetic radiation by particles much smaller than the wavelength of the incident light. Specifically, the scattering intensity $I$ is inversely proportional to the fourth power of the wavelength ($I \propto \lambda^{-4}$). Since blue light has a shorter wavelength than red light, it is scattered significantly more efficiently by the nitrogen and oxygen molecules in the atmosphere. While violet light is scattered even more, the human eye's sensitivity to blue and the solar spectral distribution result in us perceiving the skyward radiance as blue.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Chinese Column -->
        <div class="column">
            <div class="section">
                <h2>给 3 岁幼儿</h2>
                <p>天空是蓝色的，是因为阳光喜欢玩耍！当阳光到达地球时，它会撞击空气并在到处到处弹跳。蓝光很短而且很活泼，所以它在天空中到处散开来。所以，当你抬头看时，你会看到所有的蓝光都在向你跳过来！</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h2>给高中生</h2>
                <p>天空之所以是蓝色的，是因为一种瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）。阳光看起来是白色的，但它实际上是由彩虹的所有颜色组成的。当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会撞击空气中的气体分子和小微粒。蓝光的波长比红光更短、波更小。正因如此，它比其他颜色散射到更多方向上的程度，这就是为什么我们在白天看到的是蓝色的天空。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h2>给物理学博士</h2>
                <p>天空的蓝色主要是由于瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）——即电磁辐射被尺寸远小于入射光波长的粒子所散射。具体而言，散射强度 $I$ 与波长的四次方成反比（$I \propto \lambda^{-4}$）。由于蓝光的波长比红光短，它被大气中的氮气和氧分子散射的效率高得多。虽然紫光的散射更加严重，但人眼对蓝色的敏感性以及太阳光谱的分布使得我们将天空的辐射感知为蓝色。</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer id="author">Created by Dr. Jennifer Robins - 2026</footer>

